# FE-OPS-DOCKER-CONTEXT-001: generated QA/build artifact trees. `docker
# build`'s context is whatever this file allows through regardless of git
# status -- without a rule broad enough to cover them, `Dockerfile`'s
# `COPY . .` picks up every alternate `.next-*` build output any QA/dev
# run has ever left behind (a real Docker context transfer this session
# hit 894MB from exactly this). Every isolated/disposable build uses its
# own `.next-<label>` scratch dist-dir naming convention
# (BESAT_NEXT_DIST_DIR) -- playwright, qg, qa, seo, and whatever the next
# one is called -- so a single glob covering the whole `.next-*` family
# (matching frontend/.gitignore's own equivalent fix) replaces the
# previous exact-prefix list, which had already been caught out once
# (only .next-playwright-*/.next-qg-* were listed; .next-qa-*/.next-seo-*
# were never added after the fact) and would keep needing another entry
# for every future naming convention otherwise.
.next-*
.next-*.tsconfig.json
playwright-report/
playwright-report-real-django/
test-results/
test-results-real-django/
.agents/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

.idea/
.vscode/

# OPS-MOCK-SEED-CREDENTIALS-001: mock-database.seed.json (tracked in git)
# and its runtime-generated sibling mock-database.local.json both hold
# plaintext demo account passwords for the dev-only mock backend
# (src/lib/mock-api/store.ts). This Dockerfile's `COPY . .` would
# otherwise ship them into every built image regardless of environment.
# The mock backend can never actually activate here anyway --
# lib/api/client.ts's getApiBaseUrl() rejects a loopback/private resolved
# origin (which mock mode's own fallback is) whenever NODE_ENV is
# "production", and this image always sets NODE_ENV=production -- so
# excluding the directory only removes dead weight and an unnecessary
# credential-disclosure surface, it does not change any code path this
# image's `next start` can actually reach.
data/